This is writer Steven Johnson, author of the book, How We Got To Now. He says the problem isn't so much the heat, but the moisture in the air, which was warping the paper and throwing the print out of alignment. And so they hire a young, enterprising engineer by the name of Willis Carrier to solve this problem
这位是作家史蒂文·约翰逊，他是《我们是如何走到今天的》一书的作者。他说，问题不在于热，而在于空气中的水分，这导致纸张变形，印刷错位。于是，他们聘请了一位年轻且富有进取心的工程师，名叫威利斯·开利来解决这个问题。

3
