and basically pull the moisture out of the air inside the printing plant. And Carrier develops a system that pumps air over cold metal coils. And it works. It pulls the moisture out of the air and the magazines are printed more efficiently and the inks don't run. But it has a side effect of of as it's pulling the moisture out of the air, it also makes the air cooler. And so of course, everybody wants to have lunch in the room with his new machine.
基本上就是把印刷厂内的空气水分抽走。开利开发了一种系统，将空气吹过冷的金属盘管。这招奏效了。它抽走了空气中的水分，杂志印刷得更高效，油墨也不会晕染。但它有一个副作用，在抽走水分的同时，空气也变凉了。于是，当然，每个人都想在有他那台新机器的房间里吃午饭。

