so many stories of technology really a story about miniaturization of taking something that was really big and shrinking it down. Early AC systems were massive, way too big for an individual home. But by the late 1940s, carrier and other companies were selling air conditioners that could fit in your window. But they were expensive. And it wasn't clear at first that people would buy them. I think advertising played a huge role in the increased use of air conditioning in the
