to live in, particularly during the summer months, that suddenly because of these home air conditioning units are now actually delightful places to live. The population of states like Arizona and Florida exploded. So in that period, after the introduction of home air conditioning, there is this really arguably one of the largest migrations of people in the history of the United States, moving from the north to the south to what we now call the the sun belt. If you could air condition your way through the summer, then living in the middle of a desert or a humid swamp was no big deal. In just 10 years Tucson went from 45,000 people to 210,000 people. In the same decade, Houston almost doubled its population.
居住，特别是在夏季，现在因为这些家用空调机，实际上变成了令人愉悦的居住地。亚利桑那州和佛罗里达州等州的人口激增。因此，在引入家用空调后的那段时间里，这可以说是美国历史上最大规模的人口迁移之一，从北方迁移到南方，迁移到我们现在所说的“阳光地带”。如果你能通过空调度过夏天，那么住在沙漠或潮湿的沼泽中间就没什么大不了的。在短短10年内，图森的人口从4.5万增加到21万。在同一个十年里，休斯顿的人口几乎翻了一番。

