that didn't exist before. And that coalition is really crucial to Reagan's successful bid for the presidency in 1980. There were obviously a lot of different factors that led to Reagan's election. But I think that had air conditioning not been invented. Reagan might still have gotten elected, but he would have required a different political coalition to make it possible. The population of the Sun Belt boomed with the advent of air conditioning. But it's not as if no one lived in these places before AC. Those who did had developed lots of strategies to beat the heat,
这是以前不存在的。而那个联盟对里根在1980年成功竞选总统至关重要。显然，导致里根当选的因素有很多。但我认为，如果空调没有被发明出来，里根可能仍然会当选，但他需要一个不同的政治联盟才能实现。阳光地带的人口随着空调的出现而激增。但这并不是说在空调出现之前没有人住在这些地方。那些住在那里的人已经发展出了许多应对高温的策略，

