00:08:15.000 --> 00:08:52.000
including forms of vernacular architecture that were carefully attuned to the climate. Vernacular refers to traditional architecture that develops in a particular place and it's often driven by local environmental conditions. So if you look at traditional buildings and hot climates, so many of the elements are going to be different if you're in a hot, drier, hot humid climate. In the desert southwest, houses were traditionally built with hefty materials like a doby and stone that can absorb heat. You're soaking up the heat during the day, keeping it from getting inside, and then releasing it to the colder air at night.
包括精心适应气候的本土建筑形式。本土建筑是指在特定地区发展起来的传统建筑，通常由当地环境条件驱动。所以如果你看看炎热气候下的传统建筑，如果你处于炎热干燥或炎热潮湿的气候中，许多元素都会有所不同。在沙漠西南部，房屋传统上是用土坯和石头等厚重的材料建造的，可以吸收热量。白天吸收热量，防止热量进入室内，然后在晚上将其释放到较冷的空气中。

18
00:08:52.000 --> 00:09:46.000
Homes in the southwest also tended to have flat roofs and small windows that could be closed up during the day and opened at night to let the cool air in. However, in the humid southeast, the vernacular architecture tried to maximize shade and air movement. There were screened in sleeping porches, breezeways between rooms, and cupolas in the roof to draw cool air up through the house. You tend to have much larger windows, much larger, operable windows, so the entire facade could be opened up. You might have much larger shaded porches and balconies, so there's a lot of outdoor living. And so you can look at the architecture and it says something about the place. Andaman Coldair freed architects from the challenge of designing a home that was uniquely suited to the climate around it. And as we got more mechanical systems
西南地区的房屋也倾向于有平屋顶和小窗户，白天可以关闭，晚上打开以让凉爽的空气进入。然而，在潮湿的东南部，本土建筑试图最大限度地利用遮阳和空气流动。有带纱窗的睡眠门廊、房间之间的通风廊，以及屋顶上的圆顶，将凉爽的空气向上吸入整个房子。你往往会有更大的窗户，更大的可操作窗户，这样整个立面都可以打开。你可能会有更大的遮阳门廊和阳台，所以有很多户外生活。所以你可以看看建筑，它说明了一些关于这个地方的事情。而空调将建筑师从设计独特适应周围气候的房屋的挑战中解放了出来。随着我们拥有了更多的机械系统

