00:10:39.000 --> 00:11:18.000
But AC enabled the mass production of affordable homes that could exist in many different climate zones. Air conditioning didn't just change residential architecture. It revolutionized the design of skyscrapers, schools, and office buildings. Before air conditioning, the only source of cool air was the outdoors. And so, offices usually had high ceilings and lots of windows that people could open. And so, all offices had at least one wall that was exposed to the perimeter. You might have court guards in the center of buildings so that even the spaces that weren't on the street would have access to the air and light on the inside.
但空调实现了可以在许多不同气候区存在的经济适用房的批量生产。空调不仅改变了住宅建筑。它彻底改变了摩天大楼、学校和办公楼的设计。在空调出现之前，凉爽空气的唯一来源是户外。因此，办公室通常有高高的天花板和许多人们可以打开的窗户。因此，所有办公室至少有一面墙暴露在周边。你可能会在建筑中心有庭院，这样即使是不在街道上的空间也能获得内部的空气和光线。

